    "text": "FAQ\nGot questions? We've got answers.\nIs it free?\nIgnite’s mission is to keep practical life skills learning free. The Summer 2026 program was free, and the developing courses are planned as free learning opportunities.\nHow long is the program?\nThe planned live (synchronous) format is two weeks. Independent (asynchronous) course lengths vary: Resilience & Stress-Management is five weeks, several courses are six weeks, and Physics & Astronomy is eight weeks. Economics & Financial Literacy has 40 hours of work. Check each course description for its planned length. These are course plans, not an announced schedule. The three-week Summer 2026 cycle is a past program.\nWhat’s the time commitment?\nLive: Five 60-minute sessions per week, Monday through Friday, plus course-specific work outside class. Independent: Course lengths and workloads vary. Published course plans include five-, six-, and eight-week courses, plus a 40-hour economics course. See individual descriptions for details.\nWhich courses are available?\nThe catalog contains 23 courses in development: 3 live and 20 independent. These courses are in development. Launch dates, class schedules, and student enrollment details have not been confirmed.\nWho are the courses for?\nIgnite welcomes all students. Bring your curiosity and a willingness to learn.\nIs experience required?\nRequirements vary by course. Introduction to Physics & Astronomy needs no previous experience or advanced math. Introduction to Differential Calculus requires at least Algebra 2, extremely strong algebra skills, and proficiency in functions and trigonometry. Check the individual course descriptions for prerequisites.\nWho are the mentors?\nIgnite is student-led. High school mentors helped students practice skills during Summer 2026. Teaching and feedback arrangements for developing courses are still being planned.\nWhere will learning happen?\nBoth formats are planned for online learning. Independent course plans include weekly lessons, practice, quizzes, applied work, feedback, revision, and a final project. The learning hub currently opens a Moodle sign-in page.\nCan I apply now?\nA current student application link and enrollment availability have not been confirmed. The learning hub is a Moodle sign-in page. Intern applications are separate and linked on the Hiring page.\nWhat will I work toward?\nBoth draft formats build toward a final project. Course-specific completion requirements and any certificates will need to be confirmed before launch.\nHow is Ignite expanding?\nAfter Summer 2026, Ignite is working toward free online learning that combines live classes with independent courses. The goal is to help more students build useful skills, wherever they learn. AI learning support, professional curriculum review, new partnerships, and broader reach are proposals. Their launch, approval, and growth targets have not been confirmed.\nHow do I contact you?\nEmail ignitefindyourfire@gmail.com with questions about the program or eligibility.\nStill Have Questions?\nSend us an email and we will get back to you as soon as we can.\nEmail Us"
